2013 Hong Kong China a satellite spots  an odd yellow floating object in the  harbor totally out of place with its  surroundings so what is this thing it's  big it's yellow it's in the middle of  Hong Kong Harbor one of the busiest  ports in the world it bears no  resemblance to any of the neighboring  boats  looking at the image I've got no idea  what this is this is a pretty unusual  round blob in the middle of Hong Kong  harbour  what on earth could it be if you see a  large yellow object bobbing around in  the ocean there's a good chance it's a  piece of weather recording equipment we  have 1200 weather buoys stationed all  around the world's oceans if I were to  suddenly see something in an unusual  place that's big and yellow my first  inclination would be yes probably a  broken away weather buoy these  specialized buoys gather data on ocean  currents and temperatures to help  forecasters predict weather patterns we  can track them so even if they break  free we can follow where they are and be  able to determine where their precise  location is but there are no records of  missing weather buoys in the area at the  time the image was taken their sheer  size makes them hard to lose weather  buoys are actually quite large but in  the middle of a harbor can't be that has  to be something else  Digital enhancement of the image reveals  the mystery object looks surprisingly  familiar it is a giant rubber duck big  enough to be seen from space  [Music]  Hong Kong's floating duck is a giant art  installation by Dutch artist Florentine  Hofmann  since 2007 the Ducks have been shown all  around the world when one came to Hong  Kong more than eight million people went  to see it this was probably one of the  craziest cases I've ever had to look at  but it was one of the most fun we're  gonna need a bigger bath
 

